    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2HBvg9rAnd4CKXNEFXyzUer)_\n\n## Summary\n\nThe dashboard read every agenda file through Org at each start and redraw. It now keeps each file's open TODOs in `sp-cache-dir` (`dashboard-entries.eld`), keyed by path + mtime + size.\n\n- Only new or changed files are read at start; deleted files are dropped; the cache is dropped when `org-todo-keywords` changes.\n- Deadline/scheduled are cached as absolute days and made relative on read, so they do not go stale overnight.\n- A changed file is read from disk in a temp buffer (no mode hooks, nothing left open): `org-map-entries` on a file name reuses an open buffer, which could put an older version in the cache. A buffer with unsaved edits is read instead and not cached.\n- The per-draw `sp-dashboard--entries-cache` and the public/private filtering in `sp-dashboard--todos` are unchanged.\n- Message: `[dashboard] read 100 agenda files: 99 cached, 1 re-read, in 0.01s`.\n- `M-x sp-dashboard-clear-entries-cache` resets it.\n\n## Findings\n\n**Coverage (100 agenda files from the running Emacs).** `org-map-entries` finds 362 keyword headings (339 open, 23 done). org-ql `(todo)` finds the same 339 plus 3 TODOs under a `* Archive :ARCHIVE:` heading, which the dashboard skips on purpose; with `(not (tags \"ARCHIVE\"))` the two match exactly. The file with its own `#+TODO: OPEN | ANSWERED` is read correctly by both. vulpea.db has only 35 todo rows (it indexes only headings with an ID), so it cannot be the source.\n\n**Engine speed.** org-ql is not meaningfully faster: cold 2.5–3.4 s against 2.5–2.9 s for `org-map-entries`, almost all of it visiting the files. Warm it was 0.02–0.04 s against 0.05–0.07 s, possibly its own cache. The cache therefore keeps `org-map-entries` (no extra package).\n\n## Before / after (100 files, 339 entries, Emacs 31.1 batch `-Q`, so no real org-mode hooks)\n\n| Case | Time | GC |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before, cold | 2.5–3.1 s | 2 GCs, 0.03–0.04 s |\n| Before, warm (buffers open) | 0.05–0.10 s | 0–1 GC |\n| After, first start (no cache file) | 1.21 s | 3 GCs, 0.06 s |\n| After, all files cached | 0.00–0.01 s | none |\n| After, one file changed | 0.50 s | 1 GC, 0.02 s |\n\nCache file: 98 KB.\n\n## Tests\n\n7 ERT tests (`tests/sp-dashboard-entries-test.el`): hit, persistence, changed file, deleted file, keyword change, relative days, archived/unsaved. Run in Emacs 31.1 batch. Not seen in the interactive dashboard; the figures above do not include the org-mode hooks of the real configuration.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
